course: dictionary
lesson: 15195
title: An old word: seel
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Seel is an old, rare word. You will mostly meet it in old books, poems and stories about falconry, which is training hunting birds. You may never need to use it, but knowing it helps when you read old texts.
explain: In falconry, to seel a hawk meant to sew its eyelids shut for a while so that it would calm down and become tame. People do not do this today, and it is thought to be cruel. The context of a falconry text will tell you this.
explain: In poetry, seel can mean to close someone's eyes, which means to blind them. «The witch swore she would seel the knight, so that he could never find the path.» The words so that he could never find the path are your clue: he cannot see, so seel means to blind him.
explain: Seel sounds like seal, which is a common word for an animal, and also means to close something tightly. If you see seel in a modern text, check whether it is a spelling mistake for seal. The meaning around the word will tell you which one is right.
fact: «Seel» is a verb, so it describes an action: to seel, seels, seeled, seeling.
fact: «Seel» is old and rare, so you will mostly find it in old books, poems and the history of falconry.
fact: In falconry, to seel a hawk meant to sew its eyelids shut for a while, to tame it.
fact: «Seel» can also mean to close someone's eyes, to blind them.
fact: «Seal» is a more common word that sounds the same; check the spelling and the meaning before you decide which word is right.
exercise: «The falconer began to seel the young hawk so that it would settle.» What does seel mean here? | To let the hawk fly free | *To sew the hawk's eyelids shut for a while | To feed the hawk a big meal | To paint the hawk's feathers
exercise: The old poem says the dark mist will seel the traveller's eyes. What does seel mean? | *To blind him, so he cannot see | To make his eyes shine brightly | To wash them clean | To sing softly to him
exercise: Mia reads «The seel pup slid onto the rock.» What is the most likely correct spelling of seel here? | steel | *seal | seed | ceiling
test: «The witch swore she would seel the knight so he could never find the path.» What does seel most likely mean? | To feed him a good supper | *To blind him, so he cannot see | To sing a song to him | To guide him home safely
test: Which word describes an old way of taming a hawk by sewing its eyelids shut? | seed | *seel | seal | ceiling
exam: Jay reads «The falcon was seeled before the hunt» in a history book. What does it mean? | *Its eyelids were sewn shut for a while to tame it | It was fed a big meal | It was given a new name | It flew over the sea
